  // runtime logs the violation, reports "Found event, previous asserts are\r
  // ignored", and still finishes successfully with a result file, which is\r
  // the only thing Tests/run.mos inspects. Verified directly: a model whose\r
  // sole statement is \`when terminal() then assert(false, "..."); end when;\`\r
  // exits 0 with a non-empty result file, while the same assert in an\r
